{"id":"arptables-restore.8","n":"arptables-restore","s":"8","src":{"u":{"pkg":"arptables","ver":"0.0.5-3","repo":"jammy/universe","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/universe/a/arptables/arptables_0.0.5-3_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/arptables-restore.8.gz","sha256":"9f6652365f507de3a12049128a775e065b0002ff783884cd80a092227ddadd2f","date":"November 7, 2013","origin":""}},"nopt":{"u":0},"desc":"Restore ARP Tables","u":[["NAME","<p>arptables-restore — Restore ARP Tables</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>arptables-restore</b></p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p><b>arptables-restore</b> is used to restore ARP Tables from data specified on STDIN or via a file as first argument. Use I/O redirection provided by your shell to read from a file</p> <dl><dt><b>arptables-restore</b></dt><dd>flushes (deletes) all previous contents of the respective ARP Table.</dd></dl>"],["BUGS","<p>None known as of arptables-0.0.4 release</p>"],["AUTHOR","<p>Jesper Dangaard Brouer &lt;brouer@redhat.com&gt;</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>arptables-save</b>(8), <b>arptables</b>(8)</p>"]]}